+# Why every field is a pill — and the real fix
+
+## What consumes `--radius-field`
+
+Scaffold-ETH 2 styles its inputs with **DaisyUI** (running on Tailwind CSS 4).
+DaisyUI 5 exposes three border-radius *design tokens* that its component classes
+read at render time:
+
+- `--radius-selector` — checkbox, toggle, badge, radio
+- `--radius-field` — **input, select, textarea, button, tab, file-input, range** ("field-shaped" controls)
+- `--radius-box` — card, modal, alert
+
+Every DaisyUI field component sets its corners from that one variable, roughly:
+
+```css
+.input, .select, .textarea, .btn, .tab {
+  border-radius: var(--radius-field);
+}
+```
+
+So `.input`, `.select`, `.textarea` don't carry a hardcoded radius — they defer to
+the token. Set the token once and *every* field in the app changes shape. That's
+the whole point of the token, and also the whole problem here.
+
+## Why `9999rem` makes pills and clips textareas
+
+`--radius-field: 9999rem` is an intentionally huge radius. A border-radius larger
+than half the element is clamped by the browser to exactly half the shorter side —
+giving fully rounded ends: a **pill**. Single-line inputs and selects become
+capsules.
+
+For a **textarea** the same enormous radius is applied to all four corners of a
+tall, multi-line box. The rounding arcs are so large they cut deep into the
+content rectangle, so text near the corners falls outside the rounded shape and
+gets **clipped**. Same token, worse on tall elements.
+
+This isn't a Scaffold-ETH bug — it's that theme value. Stock DaisyUI ships
+`--radius-field` around `0.25rem`–`0.5rem`; someone set it to `9999rem`.
+
+## Why per-component `rounded-*` patching keeps losing
+
+Patching individual inputs with `rounded-lg` treats the symptom, not the cause.
+The token stays broken, so:
+
+1. **The default is still pill.** Every field that *doesn't* get a manual
+   `rounded-*` class inherits `var(--radius-field)` = `9999rem`. Every new form
+   field the team adds is pill-shaped by default — you can only "fix" it by
+   remembering to hand-patch it. It's whack-a-mole against the default.
+
+2. **You can't always reach the element.** Scaffold-ETH's own composed inputs
+   (`AddressInput`, `IntegerInput`, `EtherInput`, `InputBase`) render a DaisyUI
+   `.input` internally. A `rounded-lg` on the wrapper doesn't touch the inner
+   field, and these don't reliably forward a corner-radius className to it.
+
+3. **Patched fields drift.** A hardcoded `rounded-lg` is a magic constant that no
+   longer tracks the design system. When the intended field radius changes, the
+   token-driven fields move and the hand-patched ones stay frozen — so the two
+   "fixed" inputs slowly diverge from everything else instead of matching it.
+
+The token is the single source of truth; overriding it per component fights the
+system one element at a time and never wins.
+
+## The correct fix
+
+Fix the token, delete the patches.
+
+Set `--radius-field` to the value the team actually wants. The teammate already
+chose `rounded-lg` for the worst inputs, and `rounded-lg` = `0.5rem`, so match it:
+
+```css
+--radius-field: 0.5rem;
+```
+
+(Use `0.25rem` if you prefer DaisyUI's stock default / a subtler corner. Either is
+fine — just not `9999rem`.)
+
+### Every place in this file it must be applied
+
+Radius tokens are **per-theme**. Scaffold-ETH 2's `globals.css` defines *two*
+themes, each in its own `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` block — a `light` one and a
+`dark` one — and the broken value appears in **both**. Fixing only `light` leaves
+dark mode pill-shaped. Change `--radius-field` in **every**
+`@plugin "daisyui/theme"` block:
+
+```css
+@plugin "daisyui/theme" {
+  name: "light";
+  ...
+  --radius-field: 0.5rem;   /* was 9999rem */
+  ...
+}
+
+@plugin "daisyui/theme" {
+  name: "dark";
+  ...
+  --radius-field: 0.5rem;   /* was 9999rem — must match here too */
+  ...
+}
+```
+
+(If the app defines additional themes, or overrides `--radius-field` in a `:root`
+/ `[data-theme=...]` block anywhere else in the file, set it there too — search
+the whole file for `--radius-field` and make sure no `9999rem` survives.)
+
+Then remove the two `rounded-lg` patches: with the token corrected, those inputs
+inherit the right radius automatically and stay in sync with every other field,
+including all future ones.

